{"name":"Aquacade","hex":"#e1f0ea","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aquacade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An entertainment consisting of swimmers and divers performing to music"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquacade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Billy Rose's Aquacade","blocks":[{"text":"Billy Rose's Aquacade was a music, dance and swimming show produced by Billy Rose at the Great Lakes Exposition in Cleveland, Ohio during its second year, in 1937. The show featured Olympians Johnny Weissmuller, Eleanor Holm Jarret, Dick Degener, and other performers in a 5,000-seat amphitheater that could seat 2,000 diners. There was a 128 foot wide floating stage constructed on barges that could be moved to shore electrically for use as a dance floor. Dance bands such as Wayne King, Shep Fields, and Glen Gray and his Casa Loma Orchestra performed there."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/2-Billy-Rose-Aquacade-Worlds-Fair-1939.jpg/330px-2-Billy-Rose-Aquacade-Worlds-Fair-1939.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Rose's_Aquacade","wikidata":"Q16841982"},{"title":"Aquacade (satellite)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquacade, previously designated Rhyolite, was a class of SIGINT spy satellites operated by the National Reconnaissance Office for the United States Central Intelligence Agency. The National Security Agency (NSA) was also reportedly involved. The program, also known by SIGAD AFP-720 and SIGAD AFP-472, respectively, is still classified. During the same period, the Canyon SIGINT satellites were in use with an apparently somewhat different set of capabilities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Rhyolite_sat.svg/330px-Rhyolite_sat.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquacade_(satellite)","wikidata":"Q4782628"}],"im